 limits for client side operation using ``timeout`` argument of
 ``AsyncResult.get()`` function.
 
+Per-task limits can be declared on the task class (``time_limit`` /
+``soft_time_limit``) or passed when calling the task, for example
+``mytask.apply_async(time_limit=30, soft_time_limit=20)``. Limits passed
+at call time override those declared on the task class. Inside the task,
+the effective limits are available as ``self.request.time_limit`` and
+``self.request.soft_time_limit`` (both ``None`` when no limits apply).
+
